  {
   "line": 11,
   "text": "The fix: keep every output inside the range. The loudest input, speakerphones included, is point five. Times two lands right on the edge. Instead, keep the loudest peak at point eight, a fifth below the edge: that's headroom. So: times one point six. The buzz meter, counting new tones, reads zero.",
